  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home before the streetlights dim.
    - Resident returning from the university.
    - Picking up a coat for the winter.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Checking on the emergency water rations at home.
    - Checking on the water supply at home.
    - Seeking shelter from the low-hanging fog.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Seeking refuge from the falling ash.
    - Returning to my dorm.
    - Attending my final lectures.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to a dorm that was demolished.
    - Buying groceries at the post office.
    - Visiting a neighbor who left last week.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning to a floor that isn't there.
    - Looking for the sun in the basement.
    - Meeting someone who hasn't been born.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to watch the walls disappear.
    - To help the shadows fold the laundry.
    - I need to find the seam in the world.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - The paint is peeling on your booth. Just noticed.
    - Is the air always this thick? It feels... heavy today.
    - "I\u2019m just heading back. I have a lot of reading to do."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I saw a tree turn gray while I was walking. It was quite pretty.
    - The static on the TV... if you stare, it looks like snow.
    - Everything is starting to look like a photograph. Very still.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019m going to watch the sunset. I think it\u2019s the last one."
    - Do you feel the world getting thinner? I can see right through it.
    - "The silence is beautiful. It\u2019s the most honest thing we have."
