  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 814125b8ad108c143a8ceebb281d8fa3, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The school. I teach the younger children. Or I did.
    midDaysAnswer: The school has been closed. I was checking on a few of my students.
    finalDaysAnswer: I've been looking for somewhere safe. I don't know if it exists.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I haven't gone out in four days. I've been cataloguing.
      There are patterns I can't stop seeing.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The school. Classes are still running. I had a full day.
      Everything is perfectly normal. I noticed the walls though. The color is different.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Home. I haven't left. It's safer. The patterns are smaller
      when I stay still.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: I've been very tired. I thought it was the stress of work.
    midDaysAnswer: My hair has been falling out. The doctor said not to worry. I
      worry.
    finalDaysAnswer: My skin bruises very easily now. I try not to bump into things.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. I feel alert. Sharp. I notice things other
      people miss. Always have. That's not a symptom, that's just how I am.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My hair is fine. I had it cut last week. Everything is
      fine. I'm taking notes on it to be sure.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My skin is completely fine. No bruising. I check every
      morning. Very methodically. I have a chart.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My mother and my younger sister.
    midDaysAnswer: My mother. My sister went to stay with friends outside the zone.
    finalDaysAnswer: My mother. She won't leave the apartment. I don't push her anymore.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I moved out last year. My mother understood.
      She knows I need to observe without interruption.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My sister and I. We're both here. My mother moved out
      last spring. It was her decision.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My mother and my sister. Both of them. All three of
      us. Nothing has changed. I wrote it down.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - The paint on your booth is peeling in the top left corner. That has been wrong
      for weeks.
    - The light in here flickers on a three-second interval. Has that always been
      the case?
    - You processed the last person seventeen seconds faster than me. Just something
      I noticed.
    midDays:
    - I have been counting the people coming through here. The number is down thirty
      percent from last week.
    - There is something wrong with the way the shadows fall in here today. The angle
      is off.
    - The intervals are getting shorter. Something is accelerating. I have the data
      if you want it.
    finalDays:
    - The patterns are all converging now. I thought finding the pattern would be
      a relief. It is not.
    - I have filled six notebooks. I do not know who they are for anymore.
    - The numbers do not stop. Even when I close my eyes. Especially then.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 2720955
